            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Karen Bleakley"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Super yummy. The kids won't eat/drink fruit smoothies so I thought this might please them and I was right. I only used one (large) banana and we still found it a little too thick, so next time I will only use one cup of ice. The kids also want to add cinnamon next time so we'll try that. I used unsweetened soy milk and think, like LatinaCook, I'll try it with almond butter as well. Very versatile recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2013-03-18T05:11:17.033Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ashlyn Alvey"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Like many comments have suggested, I used frozen banana chunks and took out the ice so it's not watered down at all. I also used almond milk instead of regular milk. I only did 1 cup of that instead of 2 because I know almond milk is a little more watery. Tastes perfect!!!",
            "datePublished": "2020-07-27T15:46:18.717Z"
          },
          {
